WEBVTT

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:32.470
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:45.750
<b>Eight
Five
Five</b>

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:41.950
<b>The Traitorous Building 5</b>

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:45.750
There you go.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:47.750
Don't take it off, Number 58.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.640
I know I can't take it off anyway.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:53.530
Why don't you go running 
with the other inmates?

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:58.370
By the way, when will you 
be able to fight me today, sir?

00:01:58.370 --> 00:02:01.510
After I finish these documents, I guess.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:03.040
Understood.

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:08.020
Hey, does that talisman 
on Upa mean something?

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:11.150
That talisman suppresses his chi, supposedly.

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:14.460
They place it on everyone who can use qigong.

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:17.440
Upa has especially powerful chi,

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.370
so they replace his regularly.

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:20.660
Huh...

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:24.810
What is he doing?

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.920
You mean Qi? Who knows?

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:28.660
He probably pretended 
to be sick or something.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:31.390
Wow, he's trash.

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:33.110
Yeah, he is trash.

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:35.100
I can hear everything you're saying!

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:40.660
You're losing speed, you two!

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:43.160
Don't use qigong!

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:45.220
We're supposed to be running right now.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:47.930
I'm fighting Samon-san later,

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:50.440
so I don't want to waste my strength.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:51.440
What?!

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:54.360
He's supposed to fight me today!

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:57.190
I asked him last week.

00:02:57.190 --> 00:02:58.040
Hey! Damn it!

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:00.500
Don't fight while I'm standing between you!

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:06.120
Anyway, is that supervisor really so strong?

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:07.940
You're seriously asking that?

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:11.380
He couldn't even put a scratch on Hajime 
during the New Year's Tournament,

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:14.080
so I can't imagine he's that strong.

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:17.280
Then why don't you fight him?

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:20.840
Winning against me doesn't mean squat to him.

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:24.630
Mister Building 5 Supervisor...

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:27.350
Will you fight me?

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:32.320
Me? Fight you?

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:35.020
I wanna test you to see 
if you're really strong.

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:36.360
Test me?

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:41.110
I'm supposed to fight Number 58 today.

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:44.110
He said he absolutely must, so...

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:48.990
He only knows you as the Samon-san 
who lost to Building 13's supervisor.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:53.520
Forget about that! I didn't lose!

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:55.630
I'll definitely win next time, so forget it!

00:03:56.020 --> 00:03:59.510
So? Will you fight me or not?

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:04.410
I've fought Hajime, too.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.790
I've never won, though.

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:09.640
But I'm confident in my strength and skill.

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:14.060
Just hearing Hajime's name pisses me off.

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:16.900
So what if you've fought him?!

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:21.220
<i>This supervisor really 
hates Hajime. But why?</i>

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:22.650
All right.

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:27.530
I wanted to test your skill, too.

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:32.290
Give me all you've got, or it'll be boring.

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:33.660
Huh?

00:04:33.950 --> 00:04:36.170
Maybe this could be fun?

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:38.670
You think so?

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:41.170
What an idiot.

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:46.800
What are you doing?

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:48.760
This is our first match.

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:51.460
I'm gonna test your physical ability.

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:53.560
This is all I need for that.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:57.560
Come at me with everything you've got.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:00.570
Mock me, will you?!

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:06.210
It seems Number 69 and Supervisor 
Gokuu are having a match today.

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:08.950
Watch carefully, Number 99-kun.

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:10.450
Understood.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:21.130
Damn you!

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:25.380
He even has his eyes closed!

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:31.490
He got him.

00:05:31.490 --> 00:05:33.020
That was too fast, Rock!

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:36.770
I win this round. You're too weak.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:40.020
What the... But he only poked me...

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:43.500
Don't get pissed off just 
because I closed my eyes.

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:46.320
I'm not giving you a handicap 
or anything like that.

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:48.790
It just means there's more 
than one way to fight.

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:52.950
You're not making any sense!

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:58.420
Damn it!

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:01.540
Stop messing with me!

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:04.940
He's just blindly waving his fists around.

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:06.500
What a joke.

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:09.220
I thought he was calmer now,

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:12.390
but I guess he's still quick to anger.

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:15.020
Maybe he needs more calcium.

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:17.060
Asshole!

00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:24.190
He's beyond my reach and my sight!

00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:31.300
Your moves aren't bad.

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:34.080
But you lack judgment and focus.

00:06:34.390 --> 00:06:37.980
You rely too much on your 
body size and brute force.

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:42.210
It only takes one finger to destroy your 
eyes, throat, or ears, you know.

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:44.980
Winning means defeating your opponent.

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:47.090
Never let your guard down 
under any circumstances.

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:49.990
To give it all you've got 
is the basic principle.

00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:52.330
Don't ever take a match
lightly, you little shit!

00:06:53.420 --> 00:06:55.310
That's all the lesson from me today.

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:57.100
Any questions?

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:58.200
No, sir.

00:06:58.200 --> 00:06:59.220
Good.

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:03.260
So strong...

00:07:03.260 --> 00:07:06.860
He's this strong, and yet Hajime crushed him.

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:11.170
Damn you! You said that name again!

00:07:11.170 --> 00:07:13.280
I didn't lose, damn it!

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:16.020
Your boiling point is too low!

00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:20.900
Even Number 69-kun 
couldn't lay a hand on him.

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:23.250
That supervisor's quite strong.

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:28.880
Yes. He's a top-class correctional officer.

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:31.650
You've fought him too, Yamato-dono?

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:33.080
Many times.

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:36.760
Do you offer a better challenge than Rock?

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:39.440
No. I have yet to win a match.

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:40.080
Huh?

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:44.020
He's finally started using both 
arms to fight me recently.

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:46.520
Against a man as strong as you?

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:48.720
I don't get it.

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:52.280
He says that, but Samon-san 
wasn't even fighting seriously.

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:55.280
And yet he has such spectacular talent.

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:58.440
Do you think it's because 
he's still bothered by that?

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:02.160
Nice work, Supervisor!

00:08:02.590 --> 00:08:04.880
Inori? Where the hell have you been?

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:07.960
I was having matches with some other inmates.

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:09.800
Your meeting is about to start, right?

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:12.170
Leave these guys to me.

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:15.550
You're not planning to 
slack off again, are you?

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:21.120
Oh, come on! The rookie and I are 
more than enough to handle these guys.

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:22.060
Rookie?

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:24.940
You know, the one who was 
assigned here recently?

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:26.900
Hey, over here.

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:36.700
I've been assigned to Building 5.
I am Houzuki Sanzou.

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:39.330
Please leave them to us, sir.

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:47.580
<b>Adult</b>

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:45.140
You just need to watch them.

00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:47.580
Hell, you can just pretend
you're watching them.

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:51.520
But then we wouldn't be doing our job.

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:52.720
You're too serious!

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:54.760
Whatever. I'm gonna take a nap.

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:56.090
You take care of things here.

00:08:56.580 --> 00:09:01.600
What would I say to my 
sister if she saw this?

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:11.980
Um, Hakkai-san, what should I do?

00:09:12.230 --> 00:09:15.730
Your sister is a real beauty, right?

00:09:15.730 --> 00:09:17.110
Introduce me to her sometime.

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:21.620
As I informed you earlier,

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:26.120
I've been summoned by the 
commissioner himself to attend

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:30.150
the emergency meeting at the 
police department headquarters.

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:33.140
When will you return, ma'am?

00:09:33.140 --> 00:09:38.010
I don't know the details regarding 
the meeting's agenda or duration.

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:41.260
If you were summoned,

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:45.220
the meeting must have something 
to do with this prison, right?

00:09:45.220 --> 00:09:49.940
Something very serious must be happening.

00:09:50.550 --> 00:09:54.940
What I do know is that I was told 
to bring something to the meeting.

00:09:55.380 --> 00:09:57.980
The data on certain inmates.

00:09:57.980 --> 00:09:59.900
Certain inmates?

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:03.810
Inmates Number 15 and Number 634.

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:07.940
I know, I know! I know who they are!

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:09.620
The inmate who controls fire

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:11.710
and the inmate who turns his 
hands into weapons, right?!

00:10:12.180 --> 00:10:14.710
I don't blame the commissioner 
for being concerned.

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:16.340
That's unbelievable stuff.

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:17.350
Cat!

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:20.580
You're only here as a substitute 
for Building 8's supervisor!

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:21.720
Hold your tongue!

00:10:22.020 --> 00:10:25.780
Fine. It won't happen again, Samon-senpai.

00:10:26.420 --> 00:10:29.480
Why do they want data on these two?

00:10:31.170 --> 00:10:34.860
By the way, who will be in 
charge while you're away?

00:10:35.170 --> 00:10:37.770
I'll leave everything up to the supervisors.

00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:41.210
Oh, my. That's quite the heavy responsibility.

00:10:41.210 --> 00:10:43.120
I trust you.

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:46.370
I trust all of you, the pride of Nanba.

00:10:46.650 --> 00:10:49.620
You will be the core of 
this prison while I'm away.

00:10:50.510 --> 00:10:51.630
I'm counting on you.

00:10:52.370 --> 00:10:53.630
Understood!

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:15.020
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:20.030
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:26.410
The police department 
doesn't trust us after all.

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:29.700
That's why they're not giving us any details.

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:31.370
What are you trying to say?

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:35.670
Maybe they're still wary about that incident?

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:41.800
There was a time when everyone hated 
our prison because of that incident.

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:45.620
The other prisons still 
talk about it to this day.

00:11:45.620 --> 00:11:47.310
Right, Samon-senpai?

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:48.340
Huh?

00:11:49.040 --> 00:11:50.790
I'm just saying that you,

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:53.070
who was closest to the one
behind that incident,

00:11:53.070 --> 00:11:58.680
still being here might be the reason 
why the police department is wary of us.

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:03.600
No normal person would 
want to remain here.

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:06.330
They'd worry the same thing 
might happen again.

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:08.030
Hey, cat! That's enough!

00:12:08.270 --> 00:12:11.200
Maybe you're planning to strike 
while the warden is gone, and...

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:14.100
Don't compare me to my brother! 
We're not the same!

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:15.920
Samon, calm down!

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:20.340
You think just because I'm his little 
brother, I'll do the same thing?!

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:22.900
You think we're the same person?!

00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:23.720
I don't know...

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:27.350
You're just a deputy supervisor,
so don't get cocky!

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:31.100
Deputy supervisor? You're one to talk.

00:12:32.860 --> 00:12:37.360
It's not as if you don't know why 
you became a supervisor, right?

00:12:37.720 --> 00:12:38.730
What?

00:12:39.060 --> 00:12:41.780
It's because you're his little brother,

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:43.960
former Deputy Supervisor Samon.

00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:47.770
You're not here on your own merits.

00:12:47.770 --> 00:12:50.020
It's all thanks to your big brother.

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:53.540
You only became a supervisor
to replace him, right?

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:54.500
What?!

00:12:54.740 --> 00:12:58.560
So it's only natural for people to think
that incident could happen again.

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:01.380
We don't trust you.

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:07.760
Do you know what people call your 
building behind closed doors?

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:10.010
The Traitorous Building 5.

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:11.470
What?!

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:17.600
<i>Apprehend Building 5's supervisor, Enki Gokuu!</i>

00:13:18.470 --> 00:13:20.520
<i>He's been charged with killing an inmate.</i>

00:13:21.270 --> 00:13:24.400
<i>He has murdered an inmate 
of his own building.</i>

00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:31.200
Your brother murdered an inmate.

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:35.160
I heard he even attacked the guards 
who tried to hold him down.

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:40.590
He wanted to prove his strength by baring 
his fangs against an inmate and his own peers.

00:13:41.580 --> 00:13:43.440
You're like that too, aren't you?

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:46.050
You can't stand not being number one.

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:47.610
Just like your brother!

00:13:47.610 --> 00:13:48.680
What?

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:51.880
That's why everyone keeps 
their distance from you.

00:13:51.880 --> 00:13:54.430
They think you'll betray them one day.

00:13:56.210 --> 00:13:57.360
You're wrong!

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:02.140
<i>He's wrong!</i>

00:14:02.140 --> 00:14:05.440
<i>My desired power is completely 
different from his!</i>

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:08.440
What's wrong?

00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:11.560
Aw, I hit the nail on the head, didn't I?

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:14.700
Senpai must be mentally weak.

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:18.960
That's enough!

00:14:19.240 --> 00:14:21.410
What's the big idea?!

00:14:21.410 --> 00:14:24.840
Don't make accusations when 
you weren't even there!

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:26.210
Kiji-senpai...

00:14:26.650 --> 00:14:30.470
You're just frustrated because 
Samon outranks you.

00:14:30.920 --> 00:14:33.690
You act resentful without even 
acknowledging his efforts.

00:14:33.690 --> 00:14:36.160
And on top of that, 
you've insulted his family.

00:14:36.690 --> 00:14:38.300
You're the lowest of the low!

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:45.480
<i>This is so awkward.</i>

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:48.060
Damn it!

00:14:48.060 --> 00:14:49.990
He thinks I'm the same as my brother?!

00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:54.090
Before that, all I heard was 
how different he and I were!

00:14:55.220 --> 00:14:56.290
Brother...

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:59.190
Always strive to win against yourself.

00:14:59.190 --> 00:15:02.880
That was what the former supervisor 
of The Disciplined Building 5,

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.750
my brother, used to say often.

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:08.340
Brilliant physical ability...

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:11.010
A mental strength that's never 
intimidated by any training...

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:15.460
He was indispensable to 
Building 5—to Nanba Prison.

00:15:16.700 --> 00:15:19.680
<i>Always strive to win against yourself!</i>

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:23.750
The way he held firm to the 
course he set for himself

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:26.870
influenced other correctional 
officers and inmates alike.

00:15:26.870 --> 00:15:29.780
They all wanted to surpass him.

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:32.530
I was one of them, and yet...

00:15:33.310 --> 00:15:33.950
Why?!

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:37.210
Why did he do such a thing?

00:15:37.210 --> 00:15:39.760
Oh, there you are, little monkey.

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:42.390
You didn't respond to my calls.

00:15:42.390 --> 00:15:44.640
It seems you didn't hear 
the announcement, either,

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:46.790
so I've been looking all over for you!

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:48.610
You need something?

00:15:48.610 --> 00:15:50.470
You have a visitor.

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:52.740
A visitor? For me?

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:55.720
That incredibly beautiful lady from before.

00:15:58.710 --> 00:16:01.230
It's been a long time, Samon-san.

00:16:01.450 --> 00:16:04.230
Big Sister Nori— er, Noriko-san.

00:16:04.620 --> 00:16:08.230
You can call me what you 
always used to, Samon-san.

00:16:13.560 --> 00:16:16.280
I really wanted to go all the way to Building 5,

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:18.370
but I got a little tired.

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:21.460
Don't worry. This place is too big anyway.

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:22.960
Are you doing well?

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:24.880
Yes, I'm doing pretty well.

00:16:25.650 --> 00:16:29.250
Uh, is Houzuki doing well?

00:16:29.510 --> 00:16:31.180
Houzuki? Oh!

00:16:31.710 --> 00:16:34.560
Ah, he's your...

00:16:34.560 --> 00:16:35.760
My younger brother.

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:40.240
That's right. You had never met him before.

00:16:40.240 --> 00:16:42.590
No wonder... I thought
you two looked alike.

00:16:43.220 --> 00:16:47.650
He's very shy and always 
used to hide behind me.

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:50.150
I'm surprised he got assigned here.

00:16:50.700 --> 00:16:53.300
It's probably because all of you are here.

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:55.160
Us?

00:16:55.340 --> 00:16:58.660
He admired all of you so much.

00:17:00.560 --> 00:17:02.910
He studied very hard.

00:17:03.180 --> 00:17:07.440
I see... I'll talk to him next time.

00:17:08.680 --> 00:17:11.650
Um... Is Enki-san doing well?

00:17:11.650 --> 00:17:12.170
Huh?

00:17:12.690 --> 00:17:15.680
I was unable to see him the 
last time I was here, too.

00:17:16.090 --> 00:17:19.230
The guards won't tell me 
much about him, either.

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:23.430
I thought maybe he'd gotten sick or something.

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:25.190
My brother is...

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:29.960
The supervisor had to go 
to a sudden meeting.

00:17:29.960 --> 00:17:32.280
So, being the deputy 
supervisor, I came instead.

00:17:32.750 --> 00:17:33.910
Sorry.

00:17:33.910 --> 00:17:35.380
I see.

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:38.460
But I'm glad I got to see you, at least.

00:17:39.690 --> 00:17:42.470
If you like, please share 
this with your coworkers.

00:17:42.730 --> 00:17:44.790
I'm not certain you'll like it, but...

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:52.050
I made them less sweet, since I don't 
think Enki-san likes sweets.

00:17:52.770 --> 00:17:53.890
Thanks.

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:58.330
Please take care of my little brother.

00:17:58.330 --> 00:17:59.240
Yeah.

00:17:59.240 --> 00:18:02.920
Also, please tell him I'll come visit him again.

00:18:02.920 --> 00:18:04.310
I will.

00:18:24.450 --> 00:18:26.500
For this attack, the arm's 
angle should be like this!

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:28.990
Like this?

00:18:28.990 --> 00:18:31.400
Yeah. You're a fast learner.

00:18:31.400 --> 00:18:32.130
You've got potential.

00:18:32.620 --> 00:18:34.240
Okay, let's start from the beginning.

00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:34.990
Yes, sir.

00:18:36.200 --> 00:18:38.050
I'm hungry!

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:40.140
Where did the time go?

00:18:40.600 --> 00:18:44.000
I've been moving all day.
Now I can't move a muscle!

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:46.860
I was looking forward to eating 
authentic Chinese food.

00:18:46.860 --> 00:18:51.090
Sorry. The supervisor told 
me to get back on time.

00:18:51.090 --> 00:18:52.150
Um...

00:18:52.540 --> 00:18:55.950
You came all the way from Building 13,

00:18:55.950 --> 00:18:58.060
so why don't you at least have some tea?

00:18:58.060 --> 00:18:59.320
And some snacks?

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:00.410
Yes.

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:01.840
Oh, what the heck?

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:03.900
Let's have some, since we're already here.

00:19:03.900 --> 00:19:05.660
Now you're talking!

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:10.770
Just because you're standing here

00:19:10.770 --> 00:19:13.090
doesn't mean the warden 
will return, you know.

00:19:13.670 --> 00:19:15.420
She just left.

00:19:19.100 --> 00:19:20.890
Pull yourself together.

00:19:20.890 --> 00:19:23.930
We're going to be busy 
while the warden is gone.

00:19:23.930 --> 00:19:25.140
I know that.

00:19:25.840 --> 00:19:29.830
By the way, I heard you snapped at 
the cat regarding that incident.

00:19:31.780 --> 00:19:35.350
Are you still bothered by that incident...

00:19:35.350 --> 00:19:36.810
By Enki?

00:19:36.810 --> 00:19:40.060
Oh, please. It's much simpler than all that.

00:19:40.060 --> 00:19:43.580
Doesn't it bother you when someone 
insults your colleague, too?

00:19:43.580 --> 00:19:47.780
To think Samon will betray 
us just because Enki did...

00:19:47.780 --> 00:19:49.580
That's such childish thinking.

00:19:50.820 --> 00:19:54.910
When they see Samon,
they only see a shadow of Enki.

00:19:54.910 --> 00:19:58.010
Labeling him without actually knowing him...

00:19:58.010 --> 00:20:02.090
They have no right to 
label someone like that.

00:20:02.850 --> 00:20:03.840
You're right.

00:20:04.310 --> 00:20:05.380
Of course I am.

00:20:06.630 --> 00:20:07.560
Here you go, sir.

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:12.100
Where's Yamato?

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:15.800
I believe he'll return soon...

00:20:15.800 --> 00:20:19.350
Jeez... I told him to return on time.

00:20:19.350 --> 00:20:20.360
That idiot.

00:20:20.810 --> 00:20:22.200
Um, Supervisor?

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:23.120
Hm?

00:20:23.120 --> 00:20:25.620
Did something happen to Number 15-kun?

00:20:25.900 --> 00:20:27.100
Number 15?

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:29.930
He's been acting kind of odd lately.

00:20:29.930 --> 00:20:32.320
It's not that he looks unwell, but...

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:36.140
He looks a bit dispirited,

00:20:36.140 --> 00:20:38.130
like something is bothering him.

00:20:39.280 --> 00:20:42.590
After that night when he 
tried to escape alone...

00:20:45.110 --> 00:20:48.380
It's like he's been forcing himself 
to act normal ever since.

00:20:49.120 --> 00:20:50.190
Who knows?

00:20:55.670 --> 00:20:59.180
Crap. Maybe I've come too far.

00:20:59.180 --> 00:21:01.030
I should start heading back.

00:21:06.220 --> 00:21:07.280
Rock?

00:21:11.820 --> 00:21:13.620
Deputy Supervisor, welcome back.

00:21:13.900 --> 00:21:15.100
You're late!

00:21:15.100 --> 00:21:18.000
Did Number 69 and the others
return to their cell?

00:21:19.720 --> 00:21:22.650
Hey. I heard you'd gone to Building 5.

00:21:26.140 --> 00:21:27.230
Where's Yamato?

00:21:29.620 --> 00:21:30.760
Deputy Supervisor?!

00:21:40.910 --> 00:21:42.190
Rock?

00:21:46.990 --> 00:21:50.270
Rock?!

00:23:25.040 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:26.020 --> 00:23:28.660
Rock has been acting weird ever since 
he got back from Building 5.

00:23:28.660 --> 00:23:30.220
And even Yamato, too.

00:23:30.430 --> 00:23:34.550
To find out the truth, we headed 
to Building 5 with Hajime.

00:23:34.760 --> 00:23:37.110
What was waiting for us there was...

00:23:36.600 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>Something Is Breaking</b>

00:23:37.110 --> 00:23:40.060
Next episode: "Something Is Breaking."
